  "finalText": "I built the 6-second loop: five blurred purple and teal orbs drifting slowly, over a dot grid that pulses gently. I checked it in a contact sheet at 0, 1.5, 3, 4.5 and 5.97 s, and the first and last frames match. I haven't exported or played it back.\n\n- **Orbs (**o1–o5**):** each is a large, heavily blurred ellipse in violet, indigo, lavender or teal. Each drifts a small distance on a sine/cos path with a period of exactly 6 s (some run at two cycles per 6 s). Orbs 1 and 2 also breathe slightly in scale. Because the motion comes from expressions rather than keyframes, the loop has no hard stop and no jump at the seam.\n- **Dot grid:** 12×7 small white dots in two checkerboard groups (**dotsA**, **dotsB**). Their opacity swells in opposite phase on the same 6 s cycle, so a soft shimmer ripples across the grid instead of the whole grid blinking.\n- **Background:** deep navy, `#0b0820`.\n\nI can make the drift slower or the dots stronger, shift the palette, or increase the grid density to 16×9 if you want."
